body:
I love Things 2. It has everything I need save a few things that I was sure would be implemented in Things 3. Here are my 3 gripes (so far) 

1. automatic import from Reminders
I use Siri to set my reminders and love the fact that Things gives the option to import them from the Apple Reminders app. But it needs to have an option for automatic import. Right now, the process goes:

1. &#34;Hey Siri. Remind me to do laundry&#34;
2. Open Things. 
3. Back out of &#34;Today&#34;
4. Tap into &#34;Inbox&#34;
5. Tap &#34;import all&#34;
6. Select to import to &#34;Today&#34;
7.  Back out of &#34;Inbox&#34;
8. Go back into &#34;Today&#34;

I understand that the point of making it a manual process is to ensure you don&#39;t have any reminders you want to keep in Apple Reminders. But it should definitely be an option to make all those tedious steps automatic for users who choose to make Things their exclusive to do list:

1. &#34;Hey Siri. Remind me to do laundry&#34;
2. Open Things. And there they are already in &#34;Today&#34;

2. pricing model. I already paid about $70 for the desktop/iphone/iPad versions of Things 2. I could argue that this should at least be bundled for iOS devices instead of a separates cost for iPhone and iPad.  But while a bit pricey, I came to find it was worth it. Each purchase is specifically designed for the device it&#39;s being used on. Fine, here&#39;s my ~70. With Things 3 though, not only have they stuck to that model, but they&#39;re insulting previous customers by not even offering a discount for upgrade. THIS APP ISNT THINGS 3. It&#39;s Things 2.5. Meaning, there really isn&#39;t anything, other than design that warrants asking so much  money if you already own Things 2. 

3. Maybe I&#39;m missing it, but gone are the days when I can see my Today view split into &#34;areas&#34;. Everything is just a long list jumbled together. I&#39;ll change my rating if I discover it is there, but I think they&#39;ve done away with it.
